Instrument data (fetched or built by tools/mkinstrument and tools/mkinst; never committed to this
repository, distributed separately from the source repo):

  Salamander Grand Piano v3
    (c) Alexander Holm — http://freepats.zenvoid.org/Piano/
    Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/)

    This instrument is included as a modified subset: velocity layers were reduced, the
    signal was downmixed to mono, and loop points may have been written where the source
    had none. The unmodified upstream library is also licensed under CC-BY-3.0 and remains
    freely reusable under those terms; the attribution above is supplied for that library
    and for our subset. Per CC-BY-3.0 section 4, this file is the "specified acknowledgment"
    and the statement in this paragraph is the required indication of changes.
    This is the instrument tools/mkinst cuts. tools/mkinst writes a generated NOTICE.txt into the
    instrument directory it builds, so the attribution travels with the audio, not only with the source.

  Upright Piano KW, version 2022-02-21   (the starter instrument README tells you to fetch)
    Recorded January 2017 by Gonzalo and Roberto of the FreePats project, from a Kawai upright in a
    living room - upstream credits Inma Martínez de Miguel for the piano and the room.
    http://freepats.zenvoid.org/Piano/acoustic-grand-piano.html#UprightKW
    Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/)

    CC0 needs no attribution, so this entry is a courtesy rather than a requirement. What is required
    is that the terms stay with the audio: tools/mkinstrument checks the release zip against a pinned
    sha256 and copies the upstream LICENSE and README.md next to the decoded samples.

Note: the instruments' terms - CC-BY-3.0 for Salamander, CC0 for the upright - are more permissive
than the PolyForm terms that cover Boreaz's own source. That is deliberate. The covers apply to
different material and are shipped in separate artifacts.
